 "_comment": "Hand corrections to the occupation record, applied before names are merged. Each row replaces whatever overlapped [from, to] (inclusive; use map-snapshot years) for one province, keyed Country/Region, with the given occupier. The border source leaves New York, Pennsylvania and the Carolinas with Native groups until 1782 although they were British colonies. Also: Belgium after 1815 (the source calls it Austrian) and Hamburg, which the source gives to Sweden/Hanover/Mecklenburg-Strelitz. Brittany also covers Ille-et-Vilaine (Rennes) and Loire-Atlantique (Nantes) from 900 to 1599, matching the three Breton provinces the source already marks (they were annexed from the Franks in 851). Also: French Louisiana and New France (1650-1762) and what followed (Spanish Louisiana, the British Province of Quebec and West Florida), which the source leaves as Native groups, Rupert's Land or nothing until 1783. Use 'city' to pick one province of a region that was split into several.",
